From: Pavel Bragin <pabragin@yandex.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] nvmem: layouts: u-boot-env: support mac-base cells

The layout converts only the variable named "ethaddr" into a binary MAC
address. Vendors keep further addresses under other names: Xiaomi stores
the WAN address of the BE5000 as "ethaddr_wan". Run the shared mac-base
parser on every other cell, so a cell node with compatible = "mac-base"
turns an ASCII, hex or raw value into a MAC address the same way the
fixed-layout and ascii-env layouts do.

Signed-off-by: Pavel Bragin <pabragin@yandex.ru>
---
 drivers/nvmem/layouts/u-boot-env.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/nvmem/layouts/u-boot-env.c
+++ b/drivers/nvmem/layouts/u-boot-env.c
@@ -78,6 +78,8 @@
 			info.raw_len = strlen(value);
 			info.bytes = ETH_ALEN;
 			info.read_post_process = u_boot_env_read_post_process_ethaddr;
+		} else {
+			nvmem_layout_parse_mac_base(&info);
 		}
 
 		nvmem_add_one_cell(nvmem, &info);
